WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.633
Good morning, children.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.302
I'm your new governess,
Mrs. Davenport.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.236
Too formal.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:20.310
Henry, Beatrice,
I'm so glad to meet you.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.650
I've heard so much about you,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:25.818
and I'm sure we're going to be
very good friends.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.325
Too familiar.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.825
Hello.
I'm Mrs. Davenport.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:37.359
Your father has asked me here
to be your new governess.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:40.271
Something he did
without mentioning it to us.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.002
Good morning, children.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.011
It's good to see you.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.013
You must be Henry,

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:51.074
and this... is Beatrice.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:57.889
Henry Burleigh,
Viscount Timmins.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:02.793
My sister,
the Lady Beatrice Flora.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.730
You will address us
as "milord" and "milady."

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.734
Of course, milord.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.498
Please, sit down.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.634
Let's get to know one another,
shall we?

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.143
I am Mrs. Davenport.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.375
I hope to be a friend to you
as well as a governess.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.974
In ullam
rem ne properemus.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.541
I beg your pardon?

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.986
In ullam rem ne properemus.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.547
Is your Latin a bit rusty?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.725
I... suppose it is.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.990
Then I don't see how

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.224
you'll be doing
my lessons with me.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:45.595
Milord, I assure you
that I am more than qualified

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.003
to instruct you.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.907
I may have to brush up
on my Latin,

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:53.174
but when it comes to mathematics
and the sciences,

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:57.013
I'm sure you'll find
my lessons challenging.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.986
And Beatrice...

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:05.120
...what do you like to study?

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.625
Nothing.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.787
Not even painting
or needlework?

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:13.128
I just made my first sampler.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.225
I finished it yesterday.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:18.431
Did you? Oh, I'd love
to see it sometime.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.961
I don't have it anymore.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.530
I gave it to Mother.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.768
Beatrice...

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.300
My sister is confused.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.508
She gave the sampler to Mother
before she died.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:29.708
No, I didn't.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.649
I gave it to her last night.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.616
Beatrice!

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.619
I talked to her.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.213
Beatrice is upset,
Mrs. Davenport.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.487
She hasn't yet accepted
our mother's death.

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.661
Beatrice...

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:47.598
I know it was a terrible thing
to lose your mother.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.999
She's not dead!

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.595
I saw her last night!

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.538
What have you done to my sister?

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.807
Computer, restore characters
in program Janeway Lambda-1.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.643
Unable to comply.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.444
There has been
a disruption of power

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:06.782
to energy grid Beta 4.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.945
Janeway to Bridge. Report.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.352
We're experiencing

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.152
power fluctuations on Deck 6,
Captain.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.488
Mr. Tuvok is investigating.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.117
Keep me informed.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.219
Janeway out.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.295
Tuvok to Lieutenant Torres.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:26.305
Has any equipment repair
been authorized on Deck 6?

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.636
Negative. What's going on?

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:30.802
Stand by.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.811
Be careful!

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.814
Sorry. You might have broken
the connection.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.316
Crewman Dalby,
what are you doing here?

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.979
Oh, one of the bio-neural
gel packs was malfunctioning.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.487
I had to replace it.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.887
Did you inform
Lieutenant Torres?

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.151
Well, not yet.

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.318
I was just going to take this
to Engineering for analysis.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.988
On this ship, we have a protocol
for such procedures.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.496
I was in the area,

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.999
I saw a malfunctioning gel pack,
and I fixed it.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.193
What's the problem?

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.102
Your repair interrupted
a number of ship's functions.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.263
That is the problem.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.398
I guess I'm used to doing things
a little differently.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.467
On our ship, when something
went wrong you fixed it.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.738
I would remind you, Mr. Dalby,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.939
that you are no longer
on a Maquis ship.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.608
I'm well aware of that,
Lieutenant,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:12.743
and every minute of every day
I regret it.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.777
I was just trying to do my job...
trying to help out.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.290
If that goes against
Starfleet's almighty rules,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.791
then put me in the brig.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:23.057
Otherwise, leave me alone.

00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:18.435
Captain's Log, Stardate 48846.5.

00:06:18.476 --> 00:06:20.103
Ordinarily,
the loss of a gel pack

00:06:20.144 --> 00:06:21.611
would be a minor inconvenience,

00:06:21.645 --> 00:06:23.613
but here in the Delta Quadrant,
it's a reminder

00:06:23.647 --> 00:06:26.343
of the precarious nature
of our journey.

00:06:26.383 --> 00:06:27.611
I don't understand.

00:06:27.651 --> 00:06:30.347
The gel packs have an extremely
reliable track record.

00:06:30.387 --> 00:06:32.321
It's almost impossible
to damage them.

00:06:32.356 --> 00:06:34.449
Why did this one malfunction?

00:06:34.492 --> 00:06:35.959
Unknown.

00:06:35.993 --> 00:06:37.290
Lieutenant Torres is running

00:06:37.328 --> 00:06:38.625
a materials analysis
on the gel pack.

00:06:38.662 --> 00:06:41.062
In the meantime,
the unit has been replaced.

00:06:41.098 --> 00:06:42.963
How many do we have left
in reserve?

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.058
Forty-seven.

00:06:44.101 --> 00:06:45.466
Those gel packs

00:06:45.503 --> 00:06:48.199
run half the critical systems
on this ship.

00:06:48.239 --> 00:06:50.104
Once they run out, that's it.

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.300
We can't replicate new ones.

00:06:51.342 --> 00:06:53.469
It might be possible
to switch over some systems

00:06:53.511 --> 00:06:55.979
to conventional
isolinear circuits.

00:06:56.013 --> 00:06:57.810
Good idea.
Start looking into it.

00:06:57.848 --> 00:07:00.681
There is one other matter
I wish to discuss.

00:07:00.718 --> 00:07:02.913
I am concerned
about crewman Dalby.

00:07:02.953 --> 00:07:04.921
He attempted to make
unauthorized repairs

00:07:04.955 --> 00:07:06.354
on the damaged gel pack.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.915
When I confronted him,
he lost control.

00:07:08.959 --> 00:07:10.517
How so?

00:07:10.561 --> 00:07:12.256
He became extremely angry,

00:07:12.296 --> 00:07:15.231
to the point of insubordination.

00:07:15.266 --> 00:07:17.257
Dalby...

00:07:17.301 --> 00:07:20.099
I've heard complaints
about him from others.

00:07:20.137 --> 00:07:22.264
Indeed.
This is not the first incident

00:07:22.306 --> 00:07:23.603
involving Mr. Dalby.

00:07:23.641 --> 00:07:26.269
Last week, he was found
tampering with ship's systems

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.437
to increase a friend's
replicator rations,

00:07:28.479 --> 00:07:32.074
and he has missed three
of his last ten duty shifts.

00:07:32.116 --> 00:07:34.949
Commander, you know Mr. Dalby
better than I do.

00:07:34.985 --> 00:07:37.180
Any idea
what might be bothering him?

00:07:38.656 --> 00:07:41.625
Dalby's always been
pretty aggressive.

00:07:41.659 --> 00:07:44.628
My guess is
the man's frustrated.

00:07:44.662 --> 00:07:45.959
He's not used to dealing

00:07:45.996 --> 00:07:48.294
with Starfleet
protocol and procedure.

00:07:48.332 --> 00:07:50.391
A starship cannot run
without protocols.

00:07:50.434 --> 00:07:51.635
Mr. Dalby's attitude

00:07:51.768 --> 00:07:54.328
is disrupting
this vessel's operations.

00:07:54.371 --> 00:07:55.963
What do you suggest...

00:07:56.006 --> 00:07:58.304
dragging him in front
of a disciplinary board?

00:07:58.341 --> 00:08:00.741
Perhaps that would be
the best approach.

00:08:00.777 --> 00:08:03.302
I doubt that's going to help.

00:08:03.346 --> 00:08:07.407
Dalby's not the only Maquis
who's having problems adjusting.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:11.750
And besides, it's not only
a matter of attitude.

00:08:11.788 --> 00:08:13.915
It's also
a matter of experience.

00:08:13.957 --> 00:08:15.925
It's not fair
to expect Starfleet behavior

00:08:16.026 --> 00:08:18.085
from people
who never went to the Academy.

00:08:18.128 --> 00:08:20.392
What do you propose?

00:08:21.598 --> 00:08:24.123
We need to bring some
of these people up to speed.

00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:27.102
Instruct them in how to run
a Starfleet vessel.

00:08:27.137 --> 00:08:30.436
Show them why we do things
the way we do.

00:08:30.473 --> 00:08:33.931
Give them an opportunity to feel
like they're part of the team.

00:08:33.977 --> 00:08:37.140
A crash course
in Starfleet operations.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.408
Field training.

00:08:38.448 --> 00:08:40.939
Exactly.

00:08:40.984 --> 00:08:43.282
So, what do you think,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:08:43.319 --> 00:08:46.117
Are you up to training
a group of raw cadets?

00:08:46.156 --> 00:08:47.623
Me?

00:08:47.657 --> 00:08:50.421
You taught at the Academy
for 16 years.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.223
You'd be perfect for the job.

00:08:52.262 --> 00:08:55.129
Commander Chakotay
would be a more logical choice

00:08:55.165 --> 00:08:56.291
to be their instructor.

00:08:56.332 --> 00:08:59.495
He is a Maquis, as well as
their former Captain.

00:08:59.536 --> 00:09:01.128
That's my point.

00:09:01.171 --> 00:09:02.900
He doesn't have
to earn their respect.

00:09:02.939 --> 00:09:04.600
We do.

00:09:07.277 --> 00:09:08.574
Very well, Captain.

00:09:08.611 --> 00:09:10.408
I will prepare a curriculum.

00:09:10.447 --> 00:09:12.847
Commander, pick out
the Maquis crew members

00:09:12.882 --> 00:09:15.510
you feel would benefit most
from the training.

00:09:15.552 --> 00:09:16.678
Have them report

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.585
to Lieutenant Tuvok
at the next duty shift.

00:09:18.621 --> 00:09:20.748
Right.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.758
Don't worry, Tuvok.

00:09:22.792 --> 00:09:24.885
I'll tell them
to take it easy on you.

00:09:29.699 --> 00:09:32.634
...telling me that I'm
not supposed to be there...

00:09:32.669 --> 00:09:34.933
Good morning.

00:09:34.971 --> 00:09:36.097
We have assembled here

00:09:36.139 --> 00:09:38.164
because Captain Janeway feels
you would all benefit

00:09:38.208 --> 00:09:39.937
from additional
Starfleet training.

00:09:39.976 --> 00:09:41.102
Consequently...

00:09:41.144 --> 00:09:42.771
I think we need
some clarification.

00:09:42.812 --> 00:09:45.940
Just why have we been singled
out for this... honor?

00:09:46.049 --> 00:09:47.414
The answer to that question

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.441
would seem to be self-evident,
crewman.

00:09:49.486 --> 00:09:52.649
Interrupting a senior officer
is not acceptable behavior.

00:09:52.689 --> 00:09:55.123
The purpose of this training

00:09:55.158 --> 00:09:57.126
is to familiarize you
with Starfleet protocols

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.129
so that mistakes like that
will be minimized.

00:10:00.163 --> 00:10:02.222
Still, the fact remains...

00:10:02.265 --> 00:10:03.892
That is, uh,

00:10:03.933 --> 00:10:06.493
if I may have permission
to speak, Lieutenant?

00:10:07.504 --> 00:10:08.596
Thank you.

00:10:08.638 --> 00:10:09.969
As I was saying,
the fact remains

00:10:10.006 --> 00:10:11.803
that you must have
noticed certain problems

00:10:11.841 --> 00:10:14.309
with each member
of this select group,

00:10:14.344 --> 00:10:15.470
or we wouldn't be here.

00:10:15.512 --> 00:10:17.309
I frankly can't imagine
what I might have done

00:10:17.347 --> 00:10:18.814
that warrants my inclusion.

00:10:18.848 --> 00:10:20.145
- Crewman Chell...
- In fact...

00:10:20.183 --> 00:10:22.151
your report indicates
that you are talkative,

00:10:22.185 --> 00:10:24.312
disruptive and unreliable.

00:10:24.354 --> 00:10:27.585
You promise to do tasks
which then go undone.

00:10:27.624 --> 00:10:30.650
That is a complete
exaggeration!

00:10:30.693 --> 00:10:33.526
Just yesterday, I overhauled
a servicing system...

00:10:33.563 --> 00:10:34.689
Crewman, from this point on,

00:10:34.731 --> 00:10:36.596
you will speak
only if you are spoken to.

00:10:36.633 --> 00:10:37.998
But, Lieutenant,
I'm just trying...

00:10:38.034 --> 00:10:41.128
40 laps around the cargo bay.

00:10:41.171 --> 00:10:43.105
Start running now.

00:10:43.139 --> 00:10:44.731
- But...
- 50 laps.

00:10:51.214 --> 00:10:54.445
As I was saying, this class
will adhere to standards

00:10:54.484 --> 00:10:56.349
established
for Starfleet cadets.

00:10:56.386 --> 00:10:58.183
There will be physical training

00:10:58.221 --> 00:11:00.985
and academic studies
as well as tactical situations

00:11:01.024 --> 00:11:03.219
which will be simulated
on the holodeck.

00:11:06.796 --> 00:11:09.856
Crewman, have you
been listening to me?

00:11:11.201 --> 00:11:13.726
Excuse me, I did not
hear that answer.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.397
Yes.

00:11:15.438 --> 00:11:17.963
Speak up, crewman.

00:11:18.074 --> 00:11:19.473
I said yes.

00:11:19.509 --> 00:11:21.409
From now on,
you will look at me

00:11:21.444 --> 00:11:22.934
when I am talking to you.

00:11:22.979 --> 00:11:24.105
Leave him alone.

00:11:24.147 --> 00:11:25.136
What was that?

00:11:25.181 --> 00:11:27.649
I said leave him alone.

00:11:27.684 --> 00:11:29.117
Can't you see he's just a kid?

00:11:29.152 --> 00:11:30.847
He shouldn't even be here.

00:11:30.887 --> 00:11:32.115
We think he should.

00:11:32.155 --> 00:11:33.452
You'll probably have me

00:11:33.489 --> 00:11:36.083
running 200 laps for this,
but I don't care.

00:11:36.125 --> 00:11:37.820
The problem we're having,
Lieutenant,

00:11:37.861 --> 00:11:39.624
is that this whole thing
is insulting.

00:11:39.662 --> 00:11:41.493
We didn't ask
to come aboard this ship,

00:11:41.531 --> 00:11:43.431
but we understand
the situation we're in,

00:11:43.466 --> 00:11:45.093
and we've done
the best job we can,

00:11:45.134 --> 00:11:47.466
and now you're telling us
that's not good enough.

00:11:47.503 --> 00:11:48.663
That is correct.

00:11:48.705 --> 00:11:50.730
Well, maybe that's too bad.

00:11:50.773 --> 00:11:52.866
Maybe we've done
the best that we can,

00:11:52.909 --> 00:11:54.342
and that's as good
as you're going to get.

00:11:54.377 --> 00:11:55.503
How about it?

00:11:55.545 --> 00:11:57.775
Does anybody really
want to be here?

00:11:57.814 --> 00:11:59.645
I don't have anything
to learn from him.

00:11:59.682 --> 00:12:02.116
Well, I don't think
he's going to phaser us,

00:12:02.151 --> 00:12:05.120
and frankly, I'd rather
be in the brig than in here,

00:12:05.154 --> 00:12:06.815
so let's go.

00:12:08.491 --> 00:12:11.949
Crewman, you are demonstrating
rank insubordination.

00:12:12.061 --> 00:12:14.052
I order all of you
to stay where you are.

00:12:14.097 --> 00:12:15.997
Chell!

00:12:17.166 --> 00:12:18.360
Come on.

00:12:18.401 --> 00:12:20.369
We're leaving.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.808
I don't know.

00:12:34.851 --> 00:12:37.979
Maybe it wasn't such a good idea
to leave like that.

00:12:38.021 --> 00:12:40.819
I mean, they're not just going
to let us get away with it.

00:12:40.857 --> 00:12:43.257
What are they going to do,
put us off the ship?

00:12:43.293 --> 00:12:44.988
Keep us in the brig
for 70 years?

00:12:45.028 --> 00:12:46.655
Every person on this ship
is needed.

00:12:46.696 --> 00:12:48.323
Nothing's going to happen.

00:12:48.364 --> 00:12:49.991
It's not like we're
guilty of mutiny.

00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:53.867
We'll just keep doing our jobs,
same as ever.

00:12:55.204 --> 00:12:58.696
We're just not going to jump
through any Starfleet hoops.

00:13:08.818 --> 00:13:11.787
You want to give me
your version of what happened?

00:13:11.821 --> 00:13:13.186
Commander,
we're going to live up

00:13:13.222 --> 00:13:14.780
to our responsibilities
on this ship.

00:13:14.824 --> 00:13:18.282
We're just not going to be
treated like teenage cadets.

00:13:18.328 --> 00:13:19.454
I see.

00:13:19.495 --> 00:13:21.190
It was ridiculous.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:23.960
Tuvok had Chell running laps
around the cargo bay.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.968
And he was picking on Gerron.

00:13:26.069 --> 00:13:27.934
I don't like it.

00:13:27.971 --> 00:13:29.700
Really?

00:13:29.739 --> 00:13:32.435
Look, Commander,
you know as well as I do

00:13:32.475 --> 00:13:34.636
that we're used to playing
with a different rule book.

00:13:34.677 --> 00:13:36.838
There's the Starfleet way,

00:13:36.879 --> 00:13:39.143
and there's the Maquis way.

00:13:39.182 --> 00:13:41.650
And you want to do things
the Maquis way?

00:13:41.684 --> 00:13:42.810
That's right.

00:13:42.852 --> 00:13:45.412
That's always worked for us.

00:13:55.198 --> 00:13:57.325
That's the Maquis
way, too, isn't it?

00:13:57.367 --> 00:13:59.494
And if you want to keep
doing it the Maquis way,

00:13:59.535 --> 00:14:00.832
that's fine with me.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.100
We can do that tomorrow,
the next day,

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:06.267
every day until you report
to Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:14:06.309 --> 00:14:08.937
You understand me?

00:14:08.978 --> 00:14:10.138
What?

00:14:10.179 --> 00:14:12.875
How does a Starfleet crewman
answer a question?

00:14:12.915 --> 00:14:15.816
Yes... sir.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:23.823
Does anybody else
have a problem?

00:14:45.212 --> 00:14:48.147
These are your study
assignments for next week.

00:14:48.182 --> 00:14:51.549
Please note that examinations
will be conducted randomly

00:14:51.585 --> 00:14:53.644
with no advance notice.

00:14:53.687 --> 00:14:55.985
I will now inspect
your uniforms.

00:14:56.023 --> 00:14:59.891
Crewman Henley, your head band
is certainly festive...

00:14:59.927 --> 00:15:01.155
Thank you.

00:15:01.195 --> 00:15:03.595
However, it is in
violation of regulations.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:07.623
Please check the protocol files
for recommended guidelines.

00:15:10.304 --> 00:15:12.431
What is this?

00:15:12.473 --> 00:15:15.601
It's a, uh... Kazleti design.

00:15:15.642 --> 00:15:17.769
I studied the technique
when I visited their planet.

00:15:17.811 --> 00:15:19.108
It took me weeks to learn.

00:15:19.146 --> 00:15:21.273
I know it doesn't
look complicated, but...

00:15:21.315 --> 00:15:23.442
This ornament is in violation
of the dress code.

00:15:23.484 --> 00:15:25.281
It was hidden.
You could hardly see it.

00:15:25.319 --> 00:15:28.482
You will remove it now.

00:15:32.493 --> 00:15:35.621
I know... I'll have
to take off the earring.

00:15:35.662 --> 00:15:36.788
Correct.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.458
In addition,
your boots are scuffed.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.968
From now on, you will
arrive in polished boots.

00:15:42.002 --> 00:15:44.129
Yes, sir.

00:15:45.539 --> 00:15:48.303
Do you have a problem,
Mr. Dalby?

00:15:48.342 --> 00:15:50.105
No, sir.

00:15:50.144 --> 00:15:51.668
Very well.

00:15:51.712 --> 00:15:55.113
You will all report to me
on Deck 11 at 1900 hours.

00:15:55.149 --> 00:15:56.116
Dismissed.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:57.981
What are we going to be doing?

00:15:58.018 --> 00:16:00.919
You will find that out
at 1900 hours.

00:16:00.954 --> 00:16:02.182
Dismissed.

00:16:11.198 --> 00:16:13.598
I'm going through
with this field training...

00:16:13.634 --> 00:16:14.658
as ordered,

00:16:14.701 --> 00:16:16.760
but I can't say
it's very productive.

00:16:16.803 --> 00:16:18.828
Frankly, it feels
like punishment.

00:16:18.872 --> 00:16:21.432
In other words,
you're afraid you won't make it,

00:16:21.475 --> 00:16:23.102
that you'll fail this training.

00:16:23.143 --> 00:16:24.610
Excuse me?

00:16:24.645 --> 00:16:27.808
That's not what I said
or what I'm thinking.

00:16:28.849 --> 00:16:30.817
What?

00:16:30.851 --> 00:16:32.580
You think I can't make it

00:16:32.619 --> 00:16:34.951
through
this ridiculous exercise?

00:16:34.988 --> 00:16:36.182
That's absurd.

00:16:36.223 --> 00:16:38.783
Fine, then make it through.

00:16:40.194 --> 00:16:42.628
It's another power failure.

00:16:42.663 --> 00:16:44.631
It's the gel packs again.

00:16:44.665 --> 00:16:46.132
Deck 4, Section 9-C.

00:16:46.166 --> 00:16:47.633
Bridge to Engineering.
Report.

00:16:47.668 --> 00:16:50.967
It's another malfunction
in the bio-neural circuitry.

00:16:51.004 --> 00:16:52.301
We're putting
a repair crew on it now.

00:16:52.339 --> 00:16:53.465
Torres out.

00:16:53.507 --> 00:16:54.974
Dalby, replace
the failed gel pack

00:16:55.008 --> 00:16:56.635
and check out
the adjoining circuits.

00:16:56.677 --> 00:16:57.644
Make sure we don't have

00:16:57.678 --> 00:16:59.805
some kind of cascade
feedback causing this.

00:16:59.846 --> 00:17:02.076
We can't just keep
replacing these things.

00:17:02.115 --> 00:17:04.583
Ensign, you're in charge
till I get back.

00:17:04.618 --> 00:17:06.609
I'll be in Sick Bay
if you need me.

00:17:07.688 --> 00:17:09.883
What is it?

00:17:09.923 --> 00:17:11.288
It's your new patient.

00:17:11.325 --> 00:17:14.089
It's one of the bio-neural
gel packs.

00:17:14.127 --> 00:17:15.594
Ah, yes...

00:17:15.629 --> 00:17:19.531
I'm aware of these devices,
but I've never seen one.

00:17:19.566 --> 00:17:20.931
It's malfunctioning,

00:17:20.968 --> 00:17:23.061
but I can't find anything wrong
with it mechanically.

00:17:23.103 --> 00:17:25.936
I thought that you could look
at the biological component.

00:17:25.973 --> 00:17:27.964
Interesting.

00:17:30.777 --> 00:17:32.176
Initiate the scan.

00:17:33.213 --> 00:17:35.807
Scanning beam is active.

00:17:35.849 --> 00:17:37.316
Aha.

00:17:37.351 --> 00:17:38.909
What?

00:17:38.952 --> 00:17:40.943
The patient is sick.

00:17:40.988 --> 00:17:43.752
Can you be more specific?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.280
To discuss
the patient's condition

00:17:45.325 --> 00:17:46.451
in front of the patient

00:17:46.493 --> 00:17:48.757
would be a serious breach
of professional etiquette.

00:17:48.795 --> 00:17:51.559
It's been suggested
that I cultivate

00:17:51.598 --> 00:17:54.624
a greater sensitivity
to my patients' needs.

00:17:54.668 --> 00:17:56.727
Don't worry, my little friend.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:57.634
Doctor...

00:17:57.671 --> 00:17:59.764
Very well.

00:17:59.806 --> 00:18:02.832
The biological component
of the circuit device

00:18:02.876 --> 00:18:05.572
has an infection...
a very contagious one.

00:18:05.612 --> 00:18:07.307
Is the crew in any danger?

00:18:07.347 --> 00:18:10.805
I don't detect any sign
of infection in you, Lieutenant.

00:18:10.851 --> 00:18:12.876
I suspect the contagion
is not harmful to humanoids.

00:18:12.919 --> 00:18:15.251
If it were, we probably would
have seen evidence of illness

00:18:15.289 --> 00:18:16.586
in the crew by now.

00:18:16.623 --> 00:18:18.523
But in order to protect
the ship's circuitry,

00:18:18.558 --> 00:18:20.150
you'll have to isolate
and quarantine

00:18:20.193 --> 00:18:21.285
all the affected gel packs

00:18:21.328 --> 00:18:23.193
until a treatment regimen
can be initiated.

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:25.221
I'll have to take the
forward grids off-line.

00:18:25.265 --> 00:18:26.289
We'll lose replicators,

00:18:26.333 --> 00:18:27.857
but I can reroute
primary systems.

00:18:27.901 --> 00:18:29.300
How long do you need?

00:18:29.336 --> 00:18:30.394
I don't know.

00:18:30.437 --> 00:18:31.927
Unless we find the source
of the infection,

00:18:32.039 --> 00:18:33.597
we won't be able to stop it
from spreading.

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:37.076
Okay, I'll tell the Captain.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:38.600
We'll be taking
a ten-kilometer run.

00:18:38.645 --> 00:18:40.613
I've cleared Deck 13
of personnel for the evening.

00:18:40.647 --> 00:18:43.616
Make sure your packs are secure
to avoid chafing.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:44.708
Couldn't I just carry Henley?

00:18:44.751 --> 00:18:46.616
She weighs about the same.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.755
We will get to Deck 13

00:18:51.792 --> 00:18:54.158
by using the Jefferies tubes.

00:18:54.194 --> 00:18:57.357
Well, at least
it's only two decks down.

00:18:58.432 --> 00:19:00.491
Not that way, crewman.

00:19:00.534 --> 00:19:03.560
We are getting to Deck 13
by way of the mess hall.

00:19:03.603 --> 00:19:04.865
That's on Deck 2.

00:19:04.905 --> 00:19:06.896
We'd have to crawl through
over 50 Jefferies tubes

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:07.907
to get there.

00:19:07.941 --> 00:19:09.238
Correct. I'm glad to see

00:19:09.276 --> 00:19:12.040
your knowledge of the ship's
internal structure is improving.

00:19:12.079 --> 00:19:14.775
Crewman Gerron... lead the way.

00:20:01.495 --> 00:20:03.793
Thank you.

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.457
You can stay there
as long as you like,

00:20:05.499 --> 00:20:07.296
as far as I'm concerned.

00:20:07.334 --> 00:20:10.633
This pack feels like
it's filled with latinum bricks.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:13.468
Crewman Gerron,
what is the problem up there?

00:20:13.507 --> 00:20:14.633
Keep going.

00:20:14.674 --> 00:20:18.440
Maybe he'll slip
and plunge to his death.

00:20:28.822 --> 00:20:30.414
Be my guest.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.175
All right,
the ten kilometers begin now.

00:20:59.219 --> 00:21:00.686
My legs feel like lead pipes.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.812
Don't think about it.

00:21:01.855 --> 00:21:03.186
Keep your mind
on something else.

00:21:03.223 --> 00:21:05.487
How about the pain
in my shoulders?

00:21:27.514 --> 00:21:30.813
That was a run of approximately
10.1 kilometers.

00:21:30.851 --> 00:21:32.944
That wasn't a run,
it was a death march.

00:21:32.986 --> 00:21:34.544
You may be
experiencing difficulty

00:21:34.588 --> 00:21:37.489
because I increased the gravity
on this deck by ten percent.

00:21:37.524 --> 00:21:38.855
What?!

00:21:40.827 --> 00:21:42.624
You never know what conditions
you might encounter.

00:21:42.662 --> 00:21:45.222
You must be prepared
for anything.

00:21:45.265 --> 00:21:48.801
Crewman Gerron and Chell,
you have not completed your run.

00:21:48.934 --> 00:21:52.165
By my account, we have
lapped you three times.

00:21:52.204 --> 00:21:54.900
You will finish
the ten kilometers now.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.778
We will repeat this exercise
tomorrow evening,

00:22:03.816 --> 00:22:07.479
and I will expect each one of
you to better your performance.

00:22:22.768 --> 00:22:24.633
Have you found any traces
of the bacteria?

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:27.138
I've checked the transporter
logs for the past month.

00:22:27.172 --> 00:22:28.264
There's no indication

00:22:28.307 --> 00:22:30.138
that the bio-filter
picked up anything suspicious.

00:22:30.175 --> 00:22:31.699
We stopped at that planet,
Napinne,

00:22:31.743 --> 00:22:34.109
brought on some food stores
for Neelix.

00:22:34.146 --> 00:22:35.977
Some of it looked
pretty strange.

00:22:36.014 --> 00:22:36.981
Right.

00:22:37.015 --> 00:22:38.312
Varmeliate fiber,

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:40.147
whole green putillos
and schplict.

00:22:40.185 --> 00:22:41.311
Schplict?

00:22:41.353 --> 00:22:42.650
Grakel milk.

00:22:42.688 --> 00:22:45.156
I've looked at the logs.
Everything checked out.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:47.658
Okay, let's go over
the environmental systems.

00:22:47.693 --> 00:22:50.321
Maybe we're dealing
with something airborne.

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.590
He's been at it
since before I got here.

00:22:54.633 --> 00:22:55.759
Chell...

00:22:55.801 --> 00:22:58.827
what are you doing?

00:22:58.871 --> 00:23:00.668
Mr. Tuvok ordered me

00:23:00.706 --> 00:23:03.732
to degauss
the entire transporter room.

00:23:03.775 --> 00:23:05.902
But you're using
a micro resonator.

00:23:05.944 --> 00:23:07.036
I know.

00:23:07.079 --> 00:23:09.138
Why don't you use
the magneton scanner?

00:23:09.181 --> 00:23:10.944
You'd be done in five minutes.

00:23:10.983 --> 00:23:13.110
Tuvok told him to use
the micro resonator.

00:23:13.151 --> 00:23:14.880
But he'll be at it for hours.

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:20.187
Mr. Tuvok estimated 26.3 hours.

00:23:20.225 --> 00:23:22.523
Sounds like a Tuvok estimate.

00:23:22.561 --> 00:23:24.722
Well...

00:23:24.763 --> 00:23:26.355
good luck.

00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:30.625
Oh, you missed a spot.

00:23:35.674 --> 00:23:37.471
Security Log, supplemental.

00:23:37.509 --> 00:23:40.137
I have recreated the Bridge
of Voyager on the holodeck

00:23:40.178 --> 00:23:41.907
and scheduled
a war game simulation.

00:23:41.947 --> 00:23:43.972
I am hopeful
that an exercise in teamwork

00:23:44.016 --> 00:23:46.484
will help to instill
a sense of participation

00:23:46.518 --> 00:23:47.815
among my trainees.

00:23:47.853 --> 00:23:51.482
On the Bridge we depend
on the smooth functioning

00:23:51.523 --> 00:23:53.821
of every crewman
at every station.

00:23:53.859 --> 00:23:56.794
You are the Captain's
eyes, ears and hands.

00:23:56.828 --> 00:23:59.991
You must function
as one perfectly tuned unit.

00:24:00.032 --> 00:24:03.524
Mr. Dalby, I understand
you have command experience.

00:24:03.568 --> 00:24:04.796
Yes, sir.

00:24:04.836 --> 00:24:06.064
You have the Bridge.

00:24:06.104 --> 00:24:08.436
The program will present you
with a series of random events

00:24:08.473 --> 00:24:10.737
which you and your crew
must deal with

00:24:10.776 --> 00:24:12.607
in whatever manner you see fit.

00:24:12.644 --> 00:24:13.941
I understand.

00:24:13.979 --> 00:24:16.812
The program will be initiated
when you set a course.

00:24:18.317 --> 00:24:19.284
All set?

00:24:19.318 --> 00:24:20.785
- Ready.
- Aye, sir.

00:24:20.819 --> 00:24:25.950
Mr. Chell, ahead warp six,
heading 159 mark 7.

00:24:25.991 --> 00:24:27.288
Aye, sir.

00:24:27.326 --> 00:24:29.624
Mr. Gerron,
what's the nearest star system?

00:24:29.661 --> 00:24:31.288
I'm showing a red giant system

00:24:31.330 --> 00:24:33.355
3.7 light-years
from our current position.

00:24:33.398 --> 00:24:34.456
There are eight planets,

00:24:34.499 --> 00:24:35.966
none of them M-Class.

00:24:36.001 --> 00:24:38.128
Sir, we're picking up
an automated distress call.

00:24:38.170 --> 00:24:39.467
Source?

00:24:39.504 --> 00:24:41.472
Unknown. There's a lot
of subspace interference.

00:24:41.506 --> 00:24:42.768
Gerron, can you get a fix?

00:24:42.808 --> 00:24:46.574
Sensors indicate a Ferengi ship,
heavily damaged by weapons fire.

00:24:46.611 --> 00:24:48.738
Eight life-form readings,
very faint.

00:24:48.780 --> 00:24:50.475
Hail them.

00:24:50.515 --> 00:24:52.483
They're not responding.

00:24:52.517 --> 00:24:53.677
I must point out, sir,

00:24:53.719 --> 00:24:56.688
that the Ferengi have been known
to deceive other ships

00:24:56.722 --> 00:24:58.212
by pretending to be damaged.

00:24:58.256 --> 00:24:59.951
We could be falling into a trap.

00:24:59.992 --> 00:25:04.019
We have a duty to offer
humanitarian aid if we can.

00:25:04.062 --> 00:25:07.589
Chell, change course
to intercept.

00:25:07.632 --> 00:25:08.929
Course laid in, sir.

00:25:08.967 --> 00:25:10.798
Proceed.

00:25:10.836 --> 00:25:13.100
Sir, a Romulan warbird
de-cloaking off the port bow.

00:25:13.138 --> 00:25:14.435
Red Alert.

00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:16.937
Hail them...
let them know

00:25:16.975 --> 00:25:18.169
we're on a rescue mission.

00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:19.507
They're powering up weapons.

00:25:19.544 --> 00:25:21.375
No response to the hail.

00:25:21.413 --> 00:25:22.903
Evasive maneuvers, Mr. Chell.

00:25:22.948 --> 00:25:25.212
Initiating evasive sequence,
beta 9-3.

00:25:27.586 --> 00:25:30.054
We've been hit
on the lateral phaser array.

00:25:30.088 --> 00:25:31.282
Shields at 81 percent.

00:25:31.323 --> 00:25:32.620
Arm all forward phasers.

00:25:32.657 --> 00:25:35.649
Sir, there's a second Romulan
ship de-cloaking dead ahead.

00:25:35.694 --> 00:25:37.025
It's launching torpedoes.

00:25:38.697 --> 00:25:42.326
Damage to Decks 11 through 15,
reports of casualties.

00:25:42.367 --> 00:25:43.265
Arm all photon banks.

00:25:43.301 --> 00:25:45.633
Mr. Chell,
continue use of evasive action.

00:25:45.670 --> 00:25:47.535
Henley, fire at will.

00:25:47.572 --> 00:25:48.800
Aye, sir.

00:25:49.775 --> 00:25:50.867
Shields are buckling.

00:25:50.909 --> 00:25:52.376
Hull breach on Deck 9.

00:25:52.411 --> 00:25:53.571
Keep firing, Henley.

00:25:53.612 --> 00:25:55.773
Let's do as much damage
as we can.

00:25:58.383 --> 00:26:01.352
Computer, reset program.

00:26:04.356 --> 00:26:08.884
Your first command together
was less than successful.

00:26:08.927 --> 00:26:10.690
You are all dead.

00:26:10.729 --> 00:26:13.129
It was a no-win situation.

00:26:13.165 --> 00:26:15.793
What were we supposed to do?

00:26:15.834 --> 00:26:17.699
Can anyone answer that question?

00:26:21.573 --> 00:26:24.371
I thought we went by the book.

00:26:24.409 --> 00:26:28.209
I certainly did everything
I could possibly do.

00:26:28.246 --> 00:26:32.080
My evasive action sequences
cannot be faulted.

00:26:32.117 --> 00:26:34.176
At least we went out
with our phasers firing.

00:26:34.219 --> 00:26:40.055
Mr. Gerron,
do you have something to add?

00:26:40.092 --> 00:26:41.582
What does it matter?

00:26:41.626 --> 00:26:44.618
It matters because if you do not
learn from your mistakes,

00:26:44.663 --> 00:26:46.392
you will be doomed
to repeat them.

00:26:46.431 --> 00:26:47.796
I was in command.

00:26:47.833 --> 00:26:49.300
Put the blame on me.

00:26:49.334 --> 00:26:51.564
The crew was just
following my orders.

00:26:51.603 --> 00:26:54.299
And have you reached
a conclusion as to your error?

00:26:54.339 --> 00:26:56.136
I thought I did
everything I could.

00:26:56.174 --> 00:26:58.642
We were just outgunned.

00:26:58.677 --> 00:26:59.974
I see.

00:27:00.011 --> 00:27:03.139
Did the possibility of retreat
not occur to you?

00:27:03.181 --> 00:27:04.648
Retreat?

00:27:04.683 --> 00:27:06.480
I can't believe you'd say that.

00:27:06.518 --> 00:27:08.577
The strongest tactical move
is always the one

00:27:08.620 --> 00:27:10.417
in which you will reap
the highest gain

00:27:10.455 --> 00:27:12.423
at the lowest cost.

00:27:12.457 --> 00:27:16.450
Going out with phasers firing
may seem heroic,

00:27:16.495 --> 00:27:18.895
but in the long run,
it is merely foolish.

00:27:18.930 --> 00:27:21.797
Retreat is often
the best possible option.

00:27:21.833 --> 00:27:26.770
Well, Mr. Tuvok, once more,
you've proven your point.

00:27:26.805 --> 00:27:30.707
We're just not
Starfleet material.

00:27:32.811 --> 00:27:35.302
Are we dismissed...

00:27:35.347 --> 00:27:36.814
sir?

00:27:36.848 --> 00:27:39.214
Dismissed.

00:27:39.251 --> 00:27:41.742
Computer, exit.

00:28:07.512 --> 00:28:12.347
I feel that my services
as morale officer are required.

00:28:12.384 --> 00:28:14.818
I assure you, you are wrong.

00:28:14.853 --> 00:28:16.753
Oh, really? Huh.

00:28:16.788 --> 00:28:18.585
Well, one... no cup of tea.

00:28:18.623 --> 00:28:20.750
Two... no padd.

00:28:20.792 --> 00:28:23.260
Three... you're sitting
on the opposite side

00:28:23.295 --> 00:28:24.922
from usual.

00:28:24.963 --> 00:28:26.260
All of that tells me

00:28:26.298 --> 00:28:29.096
you've got something
on your mind.

00:28:29.134 --> 00:28:31.432
And what tells me
that it's making you miserable

00:28:31.469 --> 00:28:33.767
is that cloud of doom

00:28:33.805 --> 00:28:37.605
that's rising from you
like a ground fog.

00:28:37.642 --> 00:28:40.611
I cannot imagine that there are
visible emanations

00:28:40.645 --> 00:28:42.772
which allow you
to interpret my mood.

00:28:42.814 --> 00:28:44.611
You are making wild assumptions.

00:28:44.649 --> 00:28:48.084
Uh-huh. Maquis trainees
getting you down?

00:28:50.486 --> 00:28:51.612
I do not believe

00:28:51.654 --> 00:28:54.054
they are responding
well to my instruction.

00:28:55.658 --> 00:28:58.456
What seems to be the problem?

00:28:58.494 --> 00:29:01.895
That is what I've been
trying to determine,

00:29:01.931 --> 00:29:05.367
and I'm afraid I am at a loss.

00:29:05.401 --> 00:29:08.165
I have taught literally
thousands of cadets,

00:29:08.204 --> 00:29:11.230
and I have never encountered
these difficulties.

00:29:11.273 --> 00:29:14.572
My methods are sound
and time-honored.

00:29:14.610 --> 00:29:17.545
I insist on strict adherence
to rules and protocols

00:29:17.580 --> 00:29:19.912
and never waver
from that approach.

00:29:19.949 --> 00:29:22.179
I have always been successful

00:29:22.218 --> 00:29:25.619
in honing each cadet
into a Starfleet officer.

00:29:29.458 --> 00:29:30.925
Come with me.

00:29:30.960 --> 00:29:32.621
I want to show you something.

00:29:35.231 --> 00:29:38.428
These are Keela flowers.

00:29:38.467 --> 00:29:42.267
They're beautiful
and remarkably strong.

00:29:42.304 --> 00:29:44.431
The stem is flexible.

00:29:44.473 --> 00:29:46.441
It's impossible to break.

00:29:46.475 --> 00:29:49.103
But occasionally,
on the same plant,

00:29:49.145 --> 00:29:53.275
there's a bloom whose stem
is not so flexible.

00:29:53.315 --> 00:29:54.612
Ah, here's one, see?

00:29:54.650 --> 00:29:57.278
And when the stem is brittle...

00:29:57.319 --> 00:29:59.116
it breaks.

00:29:59.155 --> 00:30:00.622
You're saying
that the Maquis crew

00:30:00.656 --> 00:30:02.624
is rigid and inflexible,

00:30:02.658 --> 00:30:06.116
that they will never
adjust to Starfleet rules.

00:30:06.162 --> 00:30:07.959
No, Mr. Vulcan.

00:30:07.997 --> 00:30:10.966
I'm saying that you are
rigid and inflexible.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:14.094
But maybe if you learn
to bend a little,

00:30:14.136 --> 00:30:17.071
you might have better
luck with your class.

00:30:17.106 --> 00:30:19.131
Those Maquis
aren't Starfleet cadets.

00:30:19.175 --> 00:30:21.143
You can't treat them
the same way.

00:30:21.177 --> 00:30:22.644
Get to know them, eh?

00:30:22.678 --> 00:30:25.977
Try to find out
what they're like inside.

00:30:26.015 --> 00:30:29.314
You might discover
a better teaching method.

00:30:29.351 --> 00:30:31.478
I am not sure
if I have the ability

00:30:31.520 --> 00:30:34.512
to find out
what they're like inside.

00:30:35.858 --> 00:30:38.292
Mr. Neelix, what is that?

00:30:40.329 --> 00:30:41.660
Ooh! Brill cheese.

00:30:41.697 --> 00:30:44.495
I made it from that schplict
we brought on board last week.

00:30:44.533 --> 00:30:47.161
Uh, Ensign Ashmore asked

00:30:47.203 --> 00:30:49.671
for something called
macaroni and cheese.

00:30:49.705 --> 00:30:51.002
Cheese.

00:30:51.040 --> 00:30:54.669
You must cultivate
bacteria to make cheese.

00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:56.701
Of course.

00:31:13.662 --> 00:31:17.962
Captain's Log, Stardate 48859.3.

00:31:18.033 --> 00:31:19.159
Lieutenant Tuvok has reported

00:31:19.201 --> 00:31:21.260
what may be
a possible explanation

00:31:21.303 --> 00:31:24.101
for the infection
in the bio-neural gel packs.

00:31:24.139 --> 00:31:26.733
I have asked Lieutenant Torres
and her team

00:31:26.775 --> 00:31:28.743
to investigate Neelix's kitchen.

00:31:28.777 --> 00:31:30.301
Get me a schematic
of the airflow patterns

00:31:30.346 --> 00:31:31.313
for the whole ship.

00:31:31.347 --> 00:31:32.974
Aye, sir.

00:31:33.015 --> 00:31:36.314
The cheese is full
of volatile bacterial spores.

00:31:36.352 --> 00:31:40.118
It has to stay isolated in this
portable containment field.

00:31:40.155 --> 00:31:41.281
What is this?

00:31:41.323 --> 00:31:43.120
That's just a Laurelian pudding.

00:31:43.158 --> 00:31:45.388
It has to simmer for four hours.

00:31:45.427 --> 00:31:49.386
The spores must have traveled
through that intake

00:31:49.431 --> 00:31:51.763
and then into
the ventilation system.

00:31:51.800 --> 00:31:53.165
Where they were disseminated
throughout the ship,

00:31:53.202 --> 00:31:56.330
subsequently infecting
the bio-neural circuitry.

00:31:56.372 --> 00:31:59.000
I feel awful about this.

00:31:59.041 --> 00:32:02.442
I assure you, I had no idea.

00:32:02.478 --> 00:32:04.446
More gel packs must be down.

00:32:04.480 --> 00:32:06.277
If this is getting
to the environmental systems,

00:32:06.315 --> 00:32:09.751
we may be in more trouble
than we thought.

00:32:09.785 --> 00:32:11.776
Neelix, this wasn't your fault.

00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:15.085
The important thing is
that we found the source.

00:32:15.124 --> 00:32:16.386
Get the cheese to Sick Bay.

00:32:16.425 --> 00:32:18.950
The Doctor should look at it
as soon as possible.

00:32:18.994 --> 00:32:20.484
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:32:25.567 --> 00:32:27.626
You may break, Mr. Dalby.

00:32:31.206 --> 00:32:32.366
Okay.

00:32:43.852 --> 00:32:45.843
Do you play pool often?

00:32:45.888 --> 00:32:47.185
Not really.

00:32:47.222 --> 00:32:49.782
I did when I was younger.

00:32:55.831 --> 00:32:57.856
Do you have a family?

00:32:57.900 --> 00:33:00.164
What is this all about?

00:33:00.202 --> 00:33:01.328
Pardon?

00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:02.894
This little exercise.

00:33:02.938 --> 00:33:05.270
Are we testing my social skills?

00:33:05.307 --> 00:33:08.333
Does Starfleet have rules
about them, too?

00:33:08.377 --> 00:33:11.608
I had thought we could
get to know each other.

00:33:11.647 --> 00:33:15.777
Perhaps then our relationship
would function more smoothly.

00:33:15.818 --> 00:33:17.581
Get to know each other?

00:33:19.154 --> 00:33:21.088
Okay...

00:33:21.123 --> 00:33:24.615
here's the brief history
of Kenneth Dalby.

00:33:24.660 --> 00:33:27.424
We lived
on the Bajoran frontier.

00:33:27.463 --> 00:33:29.124
It was a hard life.

00:33:29.164 --> 00:33:32.292
I coped by getting
into a lot of trouble.

00:33:32.334 --> 00:33:36.134
I was angry
at everybody and everything

00:33:36.171 --> 00:33:40.198
until a woman came along
who taught me about love,

00:33:40.242 --> 00:33:44.110
and for a while,
I wasn't angry anymore.

00:33:49.151 --> 00:33:52.314
Three Cardassians raped her
and smashed her skull.

00:33:52.354 --> 00:33:53.821
I joined the Maquis

00:33:53.856 --> 00:33:57.656
and tried to slaughter
as many of them as I could find.

00:33:57.693 --> 00:33:59.160
How about you?

00:33:59.194 --> 00:34:00.388
Any family?

00:34:02.297 --> 00:34:05.266
I do, but there is nothing
to report about them

00:34:05.300 --> 00:34:07.495
that would compare
with your story.

00:34:08.804 --> 00:34:11.272
I have observed
that you seem to be somewhat

00:34:11.306 --> 00:34:12.603
protective of Mr. Gerron.

00:34:12.641 --> 00:34:15.235
Have you formed
a friendship with him?

00:34:15.277 --> 00:34:17.609
No.

00:34:17.646 --> 00:34:20.444
He won't let me get close.

00:34:20.482 --> 00:34:22.677
First time I saw him,

00:34:22.718 --> 00:34:25.482
I thought I was looking
at myself at that age.

00:34:25.521 --> 00:34:27.352
I thought maybe
I could be a friend.

00:34:27.389 --> 00:34:29.516
Maybe he wouldn't turn out
the way I did.

00:34:30.559 --> 00:34:32.959
But I didn't have much luck.

00:34:33.028 --> 00:34:36.464
Then we got stuck out here.

00:34:36.498 --> 00:34:40.298
Being so far away from home
is hard on somebody that young.

00:34:40.335 --> 00:34:41.632
So I'd appreciate it

00:34:41.670 --> 00:34:43.638
if you'd try not to make him
any more miserable

00:34:43.672 --> 00:34:44.969
than he is already.

00:34:45.007 --> 00:34:48.465
Commander Chakotay specifically
recommended Mr. Gerron

00:34:48.510 --> 00:34:49.943
for this program.

00:34:49.978 --> 00:34:53.573
He felt that if the young man
were able to learn new skills,

00:34:53.615 --> 00:34:57.278
to set goals and accomplish
them, it might go a long way

00:34:57.319 --> 00:35:00.083
toward making him feel better
about himself.

00:35:00.122 --> 00:35:01.783
That's why he's in this group?

00:35:01.824 --> 00:35:04.725
It is our intention
that the experience

00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:06.694
be positive for everyone.

00:35:06.728 --> 00:35:09.925
If you say so.

00:35:09.965 --> 00:35:12.331
But understand this, Lieutenant.

00:35:15.804 --> 00:35:17.863
I don't want to get to know you,

00:35:17.906 --> 00:35:21.069
and I don't want
to be your friend.

00:35:27.483 --> 00:35:31.442
This is the most pernicious
infective agent I've ever seen.

00:35:31.487 --> 00:35:33.887
It's systematically
attacked every cell

00:35:33.922 --> 00:35:36.152
in the gel pack's
biological matrix.

00:35:36.191 --> 00:35:37.954
I've exposed it to every
anti-bacterial agent

00:35:37.993 --> 00:35:38.960
we have available.

00:35:38.994 --> 00:35:39.961
It hasn't responded.

00:35:42.998 --> 00:35:44.124
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:35:44.166 --> 00:35:45.633
Captain, what seems
to be happening?

00:35:45.667 --> 00:35:47.897
We're losing more
bio-neural circuitry, Doctor.

00:35:47.936 --> 00:35:49.494
All systems are being affected.

00:35:49.538 --> 00:35:52.473
Please, tell me you have some
good news about a treatment.

00:35:52.508 --> 00:35:55.068
I'm afraid not.
Frankly, I'm at a loss.

00:35:55.110 --> 00:35:56.077
But we'll keep trying.

00:35:56.111 --> 00:35:58.136
Please do. Janeway out.

00:35:58.180 --> 00:36:02.241
What I find curious is that
these bacteria didn't show up

00:36:02.284 --> 00:36:04.653
in any of our diagnostic scans
of the ship.

00:36:04.786 --> 00:36:07.584
But if the bacteria
didn't spread from the cheese

00:36:07.622 --> 00:36:09.920
into the ship's systems,

00:36:09.958 --> 00:36:12.756
how did the gel packs
get infected?

00:36:12.794 --> 00:36:16.525
Haven't I read that viruses
can live inside bacteria?

00:36:16.564 --> 00:36:19.431
Of course... a virus.

00:36:19.467 --> 00:36:21.526
The bacteria could be hosts
to the infectious virus.

00:36:21.569 --> 00:36:23.093
There are thousands
of viruses so small

00:36:23.138 --> 00:36:24.503
they would have
escaped detection.

00:36:24.539 --> 00:36:26.837
So maybe we should try
the anti-viral agents

00:36:26.875 --> 00:36:27.842
on the gel packs.

00:36:27.876 --> 00:36:29.935
It's certainly worth a try.

00:36:31.346 --> 00:36:33.940
I think the inertial dampeners
are malfunctioning.

00:36:33.982 --> 00:36:35.108
Along with a lot
of other things.

00:36:35.150 --> 00:36:36.117
Class dismissed.

00:36:36.151 --> 00:36:39.279
Return to your duty stations.

00:36:40.321 --> 00:36:41.948
Lieutenant?

00:36:49.664 --> 00:36:52.497
We're stuck in here.

00:36:52.534 --> 00:36:54.331
Captain, the bio-neural network
is failing sequentially.

00:36:54.369 --> 00:36:55.700
We're losing systems faster

00:36:55.737 --> 00:36:57.534
than we can compensate
with backups.

00:36:57.572 --> 00:36:59.972
What about changing over
to isolinear circuitry?

00:37:00.008 --> 00:37:01.066
Torres is working on it,

00:37:01.109 --> 00:37:02.542
but it's a long way
from being ready.

00:37:02.577 --> 00:37:04.772
It couldn't even maintain
life support at this point.

00:37:04.813 --> 00:37:06.906
Propulsion is down.

00:37:06.948 --> 00:37:08.415
Every system
on the main grid is down...

00:37:08.450 --> 00:37:10.816
communication, transporters,
turbolifts,

00:37:10.852 --> 00:37:12.217
and life support.

00:37:12.253 --> 00:37:13.914
Bridge to Engineering.

00:37:13.955 --> 00:37:15.047
Torres here, Captain.

00:37:15.090 --> 00:37:17.615
Transfer whatever power
you can to life support,

00:37:17.659 --> 00:37:19.923
and keep working
on the isolinear circuitry.

00:37:20.028 --> 00:37:21.188
Understood.

00:37:26.067 --> 00:37:28.501
The manual override
isn't working, sir.

00:37:28.536 --> 00:37:30.595
Can't get the main
cargo door open either.

00:37:30.638 --> 00:37:32.765
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:37:32.807 --> 00:37:33.933
This is Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:37:33.975 --> 00:37:36.307
Is anyone receiving
this message?

00:37:37.645 --> 00:37:39.772
It appears our duty stations
will have to do without us

00:37:39.814 --> 00:37:41.714
for the time being.

00:37:46.988 --> 00:37:49.616
Captain, life support
is failing.

00:37:49.657 --> 00:37:51.284
Deck 15 has lost all power,

00:37:51.326 --> 00:37:53.317
and Deck 7 has lost
its gravitational grid.

00:37:53.361 --> 00:37:54.623
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:37:54.662 --> 00:37:56.459
Captain,
I believe we may have something.

00:37:56.498 --> 00:37:57.795
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:37:57.832 --> 00:38:00.096
The gel packs are incapable
of responding

00:38:00.135 --> 00:38:03.161
to an infection in the same way
that humanoid organisms do.

00:38:03.204 --> 00:38:04.603
With a fever.

00:38:04.639 --> 00:38:06.266
Exactly.

00:38:06.307 --> 00:38:08.138
We've experimented
with heating the samples

00:38:08.176 --> 00:38:09.734
of bio-neural circuitry
we have here,

00:38:09.778 --> 00:38:11.109
and the results are promising.

00:38:11.146 --> 00:38:12.670
Of course,
we don't have the ability

00:38:12.714 --> 00:38:14.238
to produce
the amount of heat needed

00:38:14.282 --> 00:38:15.579
to wipe out
a shipwide infection.

00:38:15.617 --> 00:38:17.414
Janeway to Torres.

00:38:17.452 --> 00:38:19.249
Torres here.

00:38:19.287 --> 00:38:21.551
If we wanted to superheat
the gel pack system...

00:38:21.589 --> 00:38:23.420
to raise its temperature,
so to speak...

00:38:23.458 --> 00:38:24.925
how could we do it?

00:38:24.959 --> 00:38:27.189
I suppose we could infuse
the gel pack circuits

00:38:27.228 --> 00:38:30.391
with a high-energy plasma burst
from a symmetric warp field.

00:38:30.431 --> 00:38:31.921
But we'd have to generate
that heat

00:38:32.033 --> 00:38:34.058
by inverting the warp field
toward the ship.

00:38:34.102 --> 00:38:37.162
Right. We could produce
the required energy by getting

00:38:37.205 --> 00:38:38.934
the warp engines
to 80 percent of maximum

00:38:39.007 --> 00:38:40.497
while we're standing still.

00:38:40.542 --> 00:38:42.305
Then we could initiate
the plasma burst.

00:38:42.343 --> 00:38:43.435
Can we get to 80 percent

00:38:43.478 --> 00:38:45.207
with all the control failures
we have?

00:38:45.246 --> 00:38:48.409
If we reroute the emergency
power to the warp engines,

00:38:48.449 --> 00:38:50.940
it might be enough,
but it's a risky move.

00:38:50.985 --> 00:38:55.615
I'm aware of that,
but I think we have to try it.

00:38:55.657 --> 00:38:57.955
Divert all power,
including life support,

00:38:57.992 --> 00:38:59.289
to the warp engines.

00:38:59.327 --> 00:39:00.453
Aye, Captain.

00:39:00.495 --> 00:39:01.860
Mr. Paris,

00:39:01.896 --> 00:39:04.364
deactivate the nacelle
control system

00:39:04.399 --> 00:39:06.458
and prepare to engage
the warp engines.

00:39:08.636 --> 00:39:10.570
Nacelle controls deactivated.

00:39:10.605 --> 00:39:12.232
Ready to go.

00:39:12.273 --> 00:39:13.797
Do it.

00:39:20.849 --> 00:39:22.680
What's that noise?

00:39:25.119 --> 00:39:28.646
Ah. This conduit's getting
very hot.

00:39:28.690 --> 00:39:29.816
So am I.

00:39:29.858 --> 00:39:31.917
It's getting
awfully warm in here.

00:39:31.960 --> 00:39:34.485
Something's wrong, very wrong.

00:39:34.529 --> 00:39:36.497
I don't like this at all.

00:39:36.531 --> 00:39:38.761
I would surmise that the Captain
is making some effort

00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:40.267
to deal
with the systems' failures.

00:39:40.301 --> 00:39:42.929
The fact that we do not know
what that effort entails

00:39:42.971 --> 00:39:44.495
may lead us
to imagine the worst.

00:39:44.539 --> 00:39:46.439
We must not let fear
get the best of us.

00:39:49.777 --> 00:39:53.076
Mr. Gerron, it is possible
the console in the control room

00:39:53.114 --> 00:39:54.479
is still functioning.

00:39:54.515 --> 00:39:57.075
Please see if you can open
the doors from there.

00:39:57.118 --> 00:39:59.086
Yes, sir.

00:39:59.120 --> 00:40:01.088
In the meantime,
we can attempt to access

00:40:01.122 --> 00:40:03.716
one of the Jefferies tubes
through the forward bulkhead.

00:40:06.728 --> 00:40:09.959
I don't know about the bacteria,
but I'm about ready to pass out.

00:40:10.064 --> 00:40:12.225
Engines are only at 74 percent
of maximum.

00:40:12.267 --> 00:40:14.565
That's not enough
for a plasma burst.

00:40:14.602 --> 00:40:16.968
Mr. Paris,
increase antimatter flow.

00:40:19.841 --> 00:40:22.867
It's having an effect, Captain.
Temperature is at 340 kelvins.

00:40:22.911 --> 00:40:24.811
Can we get the engines
a little hotter?

00:40:24.846 --> 00:40:29.078
Mr. Paris, get us to 80 percent
of maximum... somehow.

00:40:29.117 --> 00:40:30.880
I'll try.

00:40:32.987 --> 00:40:34.648
Okay, we're at 360 kelvins.

00:40:34.689 --> 00:40:36.486
Engines are
at 79 percent of maximum.

00:40:36.524 --> 00:40:37.991
I think we can risk it.

00:40:38.059 --> 00:40:39.117
Bridge to Torres.

00:40:39.160 --> 00:40:40.855
Initiate the plasma burst.

00:40:40.895 --> 00:40:42.089
Aye, Captain, but be prepared...

00:40:42.130 --> 00:40:43.654
it might blow out
some of the conduits.

00:40:43.698 --> 00:40:45.791
Acknowledged. Go ahead.

00:40:51.172 --> 00:40:54.107
The plasma gas will become toxic
within minutes.

00:40:54.142 --> 00:40:56.133
We must leave immediately.

00:40:56.177 --> 00:40:57.337
What about Gerron?

00:41:01.015 --> 00:41:02.539
We can't leave him!

00:41:02.583 --> 00:41:03.743
Get in the Jefferies tube.

00:41:03.785 --> 00:41:06.811
I cannot risk losing any more
of you to save one man.

00:41:06.854 --> 00:41:08.617
What is that,
some kind of Starfleet rule?

00:41:08.656 --> 00:41:09.953
It is always tactically correct

00:41:10.058 --> 00:41:11.525
to sacrifice the few
for the many.

00:41:11.559 --> 00:41:13.459
I don't give a Circassian fig
what's tactically correct.

00:41:13.494 --> 00:41:14.961
I'm going back for him.

00:41:14.996 --> 00:41:17.965
This is one time when retreat
is not an option!

00:41:19.467 --> 00:41:20.832
Get in the Jefferies tube now.

00:41:23.071 --> 00:41:26.199
Mr. Dalby, I will break your arm
if you do not follow my order.

00:41:26.240 --> 00:41:27.502
I won't forget this.

00:41:27.542 --> 00:41:29.737
You're letting him die.

00:41:29.777 --> 00:41:31.108
Keep moving.

00:41:41.923 --> 00:41:43.982
Janeway to Sick Bay.
Report.

00:41:44.092 --> 00:41:46.959
Bacterial levels
are dropping, Captain.

00:41:46.995 --> 00:41:48.587
If they continue,
we should be able

00:41:48.629 --> 00:41:50.358
to purge the system
within a few minutes.

00:41:50.398 --> 00:41:51.365
Keep me informed.

00:41:51.399 --> 00:41:53.492
We need life support
back on line

00:41:53.534 --> 00:41:54.831
as soon as possible.

00:41:54.869 --> 00:41:57.633
I'll get back to you right away,
Captain.

00:42:43.351 --> 00:42:45.478
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:42:45.520 --> 00:42:47.420
Repeat, Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:42:47.455 --> 00:42:48.479
Can anyone hear me?

00:42:48.523 --> 00:42:49.649
Come in, Doctor.

00:42:49.690 --> 00:42:52.488
All of the infectious bacteria
have been destroyed.

00:42:52.527 --> 00:42:55.189
The danger of further infection
has passed.

00:42:57.899 --> 00:43:04.238
Mr. Kim... start getting
our systems back on line.

00:43:04.371 --> 00:43:07.465
Aye, Captain.

00:43:27.861 --> 00:43:29.158
Come on, come on!

00:43:47.814 --> 00:43:49.782
I think he's all right.

00:43:49.816 --> 00:43:52.944
I thought Starfleet rules
said that was

00:43:52.986 --> 00:43:56.820
an unacceptable risk,
going back to save him.

00:43:56.857 --> 00:43:58.825
It was.

00:43:58.859 --> 00:44:02.420
However, I recently realized
that there are times

00:44:02.462 --> 00:44:06.489
when it is desirable
to bend the rules.

00:44:06.533 --> 00:44:09.764
Lieutenant, if you can learn
to bend the rules,

00:44:09.803 --> 00:44:12.397
I guess we can learn
to follow them.

00:44:14.308 --> 00:44:15.434
Come on.

00:44:15.475 --> 00:44:18.137
Let's get you two to Sick Bay.
